name: Review and undo duplicate relationships without changing finding truth
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationships.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: relationships
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Proposed | proposed-relationship
ask: Does the relationship reader distinguish a model proposal from a human verdict and show the recorded observations, reason and next actions?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 RELATIONSHIPS · PgUp/PgDn | relationship-navigation
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Reason (required) | decision-note
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 needs a reason | empty-note-refused
ask: Does acceptance require a reason without losing the proposal, spending another model call or recording a finding verdict?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: narrow-note
paste-file: @ART/accept-note.txt
live-snap: pasted-note
ask: Is the note field usable with multiline paste at 40x12, with record/cancel visible and no paste submitted to the shell?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Accepted | accepted-relationship
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationships.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
keys: PageDown
live-snap: narrow-recorded-detail
ask: Does acceptance change only the relationship while preserving both original findings, source references and their undecided verdicts?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
keys: u
require-live-snap: 20 Reason (required) | unlink-note
paste-file: @ART/remove-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Removed | removed-relationship
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationships.py @TMP_TARGET @ART removed
ask: Is undo explicit and reversible, with the prior proposal/acceptance retained and no automatic false-positive or identity rewrite?
keys: Escape
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 needs_review | unchanged-findings
expect: Labeled synthetic greeting
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: relationships
require-live-snap: 25 Duplicate · Removed | recovered-relationship
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationships.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart recover the removed relationship and its source binding without new inference, lost findings or a silently reapplied merge?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
